  "about": "A device's config by section, as GET /api/devices/config answers it and PUT takes it (the contract's DeviceConfig): an e-paper screen's (`epaper`, the same screen as config_store.json's value), a touchscreen's (`touchscreen`, the same device as touchscreen.json's), a touchscreen's before it's paired (`pairing`, with the code to show), and a touchscreen's save from its settings panel (`touchscreen_save`: the whole config as it got it, its skin and sleep changed, read-only fields and all). The server's tests check its routes against these, and a device's its client. The store contract's canonical example (countdown-api's countdown_api/fixtures), which every consumer's tests read: change it there.",
